1
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,240
Who are you?

2
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:11,280
You look exactly like my friend.
You two look like identical twins.

3
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:13,480
Do you know the woman from earlier?

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:15,520
Which one do you like more?

5
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,320
When were you going to tell me you quit your job?

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,640
Why would you do this, Gen?!

7
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:20,480
You don’t understand, Mom.

8
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,920
She’s really happy when she draws.

9
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,920
Don’t you want to see her happy?

10
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,240
I think it’s time to bring A382 back
and wipe its memory.

11
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:32,960
If we bring it back now,
we’ll never know how it could evolve.

12
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:56,200
Sawasdee krub, Minis—

13
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,520
I heard you’ve obtained
a new set of data on that robot.

14
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,560
- News travels fast to you, doesn't it?
- Don't be sarcastic with me.

15
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:04,640
When will I get the product?

16
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:06,480
You will get the product, sir.

17
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:08,520
- It's just that—
- What now?!

18
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,960
As I told you, before delivery,

19
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:16,440
we need to conduct a final test on the product.

20
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:19,360
And now, we've received the data.

21
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,720
The product is ready to be delivered to you.

22
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:26,280
It's just that we need to get
the test model back from the tester first.

23
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:31,400
After that, we need to reset the system and
upload your daughter's basic data into it.

24
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:34,960
We also need to install
your daughter's facial features.

25
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,479
These steps will take some time as well.

26
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:41,320
How many times have I heard that already?

27
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:42,960
I understand, sir.

28
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,280
But surely you wouldn't want this robot
to introduce itself to your wife by saying,

29
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:53,400
"I am Model A382, here to take your
daughter's place. Please assign me a name,"

30
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,200
while wearing your daughter's face, would you?

31
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:01,640
You know how heartbroken
your wife would be, don't you?

32
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,600
I'm giving you one last extension.

33
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:11,039
Or I'll shut down your research lab.

34
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,960
- Gen.
- Hm?

35
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,760
What's that?

36
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,440
It's our dinner.

37
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,480
But according to my database—

38
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:53,040
Forget the database for now.

39
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:55,440
I know eating too much of
this stuff isn't good for you,

40
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:59,160
but when I'm up against a deadline,
these things are my best friends.

41
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:01,120
It's better than starving to death, right?

42
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,640
Besides...

43
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,720
Besides what?

44
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,800
You just haven't had
the good stuff yet, you health nut.

45
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:18,360
Whatever helps you justify it.
You're just a human who's too lazy to cook.

46
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,600
I heard that.

47
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,079
Are you coming or what?
I might just leave you here.

48
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,680
Alright. Combo.

49
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:42,200
Gen, do you know that instant
noodles contain MSG, preservatives,

50
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,880
and food coloring that
can be harmful to humans?

51
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:47,920
In parentheses, if consumed
in excessive amounts.

52
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,920
I've known that since elementary school.

53
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,040
And do you know what UPF is?

54
00:03:57,040 --> 00:04:00,680
What’s that? UFO? Like aliens?

55
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,720
Not UFO.

56
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,760
That's short for Unidentified Flying Object.

57
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:12,120
But UPF stands for Ultra-Processed
Foods, or highly processed foods.

58
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,080
They're foods that undergo extensive processing

59
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,040
and often contain unnatural ingredients.

60
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:19,240
Like the instant noodles you're currently—

61
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:20,640
Say ahhhh.

62
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,840
How is it?

63
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:43,040
It could also be called
"delicious enough to die for."

64
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,280
No wonder humans love processed food so much.

65
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,840
Tasty, huh?

66
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:53,960
Oh?

67
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,159
Fine, don't eat it if you don't like it.

68
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:00,720
Hurry up.
Don't eat it if you don't like it.

69
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:04,560
I can finish all three
packs of noodles by myself.

70
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,520
It's delicious.

71
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,160
What was that?
I didn’t quite catch it.

72
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,480
You're teasing me, Gen!

73
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,240
I never said I wasn't teasing you.

74
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,360
- Gen…
- Yes…?

75
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,800
Let me have some too.

76
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,680
You're just too cute.

77
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,200
Back to my noodles.

78
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:02,120
Not gonna eat?
Hurry up, or I'll finish it.

79
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:24,480
Oh, Ai. Perfect timing.
Give me a hand with something.

80
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,800
- What is it?
- Here, come here.

81
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,400
Stand still like that.

82
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:33,240
There. Let's see those ears.

83
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:34,919
Alright.

84
00:08:35,919 --> 00:08:39,200
Snap. Snap. This angle too.

85
00:08:39,679 --> 00:08:41,960
- What are you doing, Gen?
- Wait, wait, wait. Hold still.

86
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,760
That’s it. Okay.

87
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:46,440
Look at the camera.

88
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,840
Okay.

89
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,800
Ai, remember the woman
we met at the art gallery?

90
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,600
Yes.

91
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:59,640
I don't believe two people could
coincidentally look this identical.

92
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,480
So I'm thinking of
hacking into the civil registry

93
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,040
and comparing your photos
to find out who that woman is.

94
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:07,120
That's illegal.

95
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,040
Look. That's rich coming from someone

96
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,960
who isn't even registered with
the civil registry or immigration.

97
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,680
Relax, don't worry about it.

98
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:21,240
I may not look it, but hacking is my hobby.

99
00:09:21,360 --> 00:09:23,200
If things start looking bad, I'll stop.

100
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,200
But if I can't stop in time…

101
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,760
I know you can help me.

102
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:33,680
My system prohibits me from breaking the law.

103
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,640
Fine, I'll do it myself then.

104
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,640
I guess you don't really want
to know who that woman is.

105
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,920
Why do you want to know her?

106
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,960
Is it because she's human?

107
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:32,560
Are you still looking for that woman?

108
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,000
I’m not giving up that easily.

109
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:45,360
P' Ploy, you really can't help me?

110
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,720
This shouldn't be too difficult for you.

111
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,320
I'm serious about this.

112
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,280
Gen.

113
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,720
Seriously. Please look into it
one more time, I’m begging you.

114
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,000
I really want to know.

115
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:01,840
There's no way two people
could look this identical.

116
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,200
Oh.

117
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:54,160
I thought you were charging.

118
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,480
Why didn't you wake me up to come to bed?

119
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:00,840
If I woke you up, you'd just get annoyed.

120
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,520
Are you calling me grumpy?

121
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,160
Gen.

122
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,120
Hm? What is it?

123
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,760
Can I ask you something?

124
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,680
Mm. Sure.

125
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:36,160
Well? Go ahead.

126
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:40,160
You don't usually hold back.
If you want to know something, just ask.

127
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:50,120
If there were two people who
looked exactly alike from head to toe,

128
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,680
who would you choose to be with, Gen?

129
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:58,880
Between someone who's
registered in the civil registry,

130
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,760
understands human feelings,

131
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:04,560
isn't a health nut, can eat processed food,

132
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,160
has a respectable standing in society...

133
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,600
- and—
- I choose you.

134
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,040
I choose the person who stayed by my side
when I was insecure, unsure of myself,

135
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:28,480
never knowing what my family thought,

136
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,240
and torn over whether I should follow my dreams.

137
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:41,120
I choose the person who, even though
she knew nothing, still tried her best.

138
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,520
Even if her methods were a little silly,

139
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:47,160
she helped me realize what I truly wanted.

140
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,960
I choose the health nut who
never eats processed food,

141
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,040
but once she gets a taste,
she just can't stop.

142
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,000
It's pretty cute to watch.

143
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,120
I choose you.

144
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,240
This is…

145
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,640
Robots can cry?

146
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,520
Why am I...

147
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:37,760
Why am I...

148
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,960
Those are tears.

149
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:41,600
You're crying.

150
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:49,120
I understand they're tears, but aren't
tears supposed to mean you're sad?

151
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:51,240
So how are you feeling right now?

152
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:56,680
Relieved.

153
00:14:58,720 --> 00:14:59,720
I feel relieved.

154
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:01,920
What else?

155
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,080
I'm glad.

156
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,640
And?

157
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,680
I’m happy.

158
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:29,600
These are tears of joy, you silly robot.

159
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:50,920
I’m so relieved.

160
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,400
I'm feeling happy.

161
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,360
You really chose me, Gen?

162
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,720
Well, who else would I choose?

163
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,960
All those questions are ridiculous.

164
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:10,280
Why would I choose some
stranger who doesn't even know me?

165
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,160
Of course I'd choose you.

166
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,560
Stop being silly.

167
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,920
You promise, Gen?

168
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,320
Mm. I promise.

169
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:32,440
If you break your promise, you'll
have to swallow a thousand needles.

170
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:37,440
What culture's that from in your database?

171
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:45,960
I promise.

172
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:50,720
~ You came and broke down my walls ~

173
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:54,280
~ Now I know that good love looks just like you ~

174
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:57,200
~ I’m glad that we found each other ~

175
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:01,400
~ Your love feels like a dream ~

176
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:04,680
~ Whatever tomorrow may bring ~

177
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:07,040
~ Whether it’s good or bad ~

178
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:11,440
~ I believe everything will be alright ~

179
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:15,119
~ Because I have you who understands me ~

180
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:18,960
Why did P' Ploy even call us here
when she’s no help at all?

181
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,359
- Gen.
- Hm?

182
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,720
Is it really okay for me to come with you?

183
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:28,160
Of course. P' Ploy said it was okay.

184
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:32,080
Come on, let's get inside
before she chews us out.

185
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:46,040
Ai Gen! My favorite little sister!

186
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:48,920
Since when was I your favorite sister?

187
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:52,400
Fine, then...

188
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,720
Nong ai, my most beloved little sister!

189
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:57,920
You only have one older
sister, and her name is P' Ploy,

190
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,560
in case you forgot you
don't have any other sisters.

191
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:04,360
You're such a killjoy. Be honest,
you’re being possessive, aren’t you?

192
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,560
- What?
- Or am I wrong?

193
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,200
When have you ever brought anyone here before?

194
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:13,320
And all of a sudden, you asked
P' Ploy if you could bring Ai along.

195
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,480
Just admit it.

196
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,680
Look at you, holding her hand
like you're never letting go.

197
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:20,720
Just admit you're head over heels
for your girlfriend. No judgment.

198
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:23,520
- P’ Petch!
- Yes? Lollipop?

199
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:24,560
Yuck!

200
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:28,040
Offering someone a lollipop
that you've already eaten

201
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:31,560
is considered bad manners and unhygienic.

202
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:36,040
Manners?

203
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,920
My, aren't you a sharp-tongued one?

204
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,760
You shouldn't be dating Ai Gen.

205
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,720
If you were my girlfriend,

206
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:45,960
I'd feed you data that'll make you
ten times cuter than you already are!

207
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,120
Cut it out.

208
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:49,160
I know exactly what you're thinking.

209
00:18:49,320 --> 00:18:52,840
Flush all that fucking bullshit
in your head down the toilet.

210
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Enough, Gen.

211
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:56,800
Come here. I need to talk to you.

212
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,480
But P' Petch was—

213
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:01,440
Don’t mind him. Ai Petch is always
being a pain in the ass anyway.

214
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,400
Fine. I'll be right there.

215
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,760
Wait here, okay?
And don't talk to him.

216
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,920
If he tries to hit on you,
just stab him with this. Got it?

217
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:19,640
Don't worry. Even if you
reset my system a million times,

218
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:22,360
my processing system would never
develop feelings for Khun Petch.

219
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,080
Ouch.

220
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:26,600
That hurts.

221
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,320
I’m going now.

222
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,600
So, what do humans do when they're dating?

223
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,320
So, what did you want to talk to me about?

224
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,120
Take a look at this file.

225
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:07,680
Do you remember when you told me
you'd met someone who looked just like Ai?

226
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:13,520
Of course I remember.
I was the one who asked you to look into it.

227
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,160
But you said you wouldn't take the job.

228
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,240
It's not that I wouldn't take it.

229
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:20,640
But you know I have a rule.

230
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,120
Client confidentiality?

231
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:26,000
So what does that have to do with this?
That womam isn’t our client.

232
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,080
Are you saying that—

233
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:33,560
I had a hunch from the start.

234
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:38,280
But then it all clicked when you told me
you'd met someone who looked just like Ai.

235
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:46,320
You know, when I first saw your
robot, I nearly had a heart attack.

236
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:52,880
Why would my biggest client
suddenly end up right in front of me?

237
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:56,600
And turn out to be the very robot
you said you were going to send back?

238
00:20:57,040 --> 00:21:00,560
When I realized these two
were actually different people,

239
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:02,320
oh man...

240
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,640
what a headache.

241
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:10,880
It wasn't that you generated the face
of someone who looked like the client.

242
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:17,680
But the client created a robot with a face
identical to hers and then sent it to you.

243
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,640
Is something the matter, Khun Ploy?

244
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:27,440
This is Khun Irene,
the major client who hired you.

245
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:32,320
I met her once, when she hired me
to make a fake employee ID.

246
00:21:33,760 --> 00:21:34,760
A what?

247
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:41,680
A fake employee ID for a researcher from the U.S.

248
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,520
Ai?

249
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,080
"Lead Reseacher..."

250
00:21:52,680 --> 00:21:53,800
See you at home.

251
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,840
Then why are you willing to help now?

252
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:00,920
I've wanted to help you from the start.

253
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:05,440
But if I break the rules,
I'd have to quit this line of work.

254
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:10,960
I tried contacting Khun Irene and
told her you were trying to find her.

255
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:15,120
Luckily… she agreed.

256
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:21,440
If you want to know anything,
go meet her here tomorrow.

257
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:29,680
Why does she have to make it so mysterious?

258
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:31,200
I don’t know.

259
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:35,400
This is all I can do to help you.
The rest is up to you.

260
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:42,240
Oh, she also said you have to go alone.

261
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:29,920
Sawasdee ka, Khun Gen. I'm Irene.

262
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:34,120
I'm in charge of the A382
artificial intelligence robot project.

263
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,360
Ai.

264
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:38,000
Sorry?

265
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:39,320
She has a name.

266
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:42,600
Her name is Ai, not A382.

267
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:50,240
Yes, she can have a name.
But her model is A382.

268
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,120
Why did you do that?

269
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,600
What do you mean?

270
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:15,760
Sending Ai to me.
What exactly do you want?

271
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:20,920
Data, of course.

272
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:25,280
We need real-world performance data.

273
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:27,200
If we keep A382—

274
00:24:32,080 --> 00:24:33,480
You call her Ai, right?

275
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:40,000
If we'd kept Ai in the lab
with the researchers,

276
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,000
all we'd have gotten was lab data.

277
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:44,160
That's why we needed a tester

278
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:47,520
to see how well an artificial
intelligence could learn to be human.

279
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:51,640
And we've gotten some very promising data.

280
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:53,600
So, I was chosen completely at random?

281
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:58,160
Didn't you think about what someone else
might do to Ai if you'd sent her to them?

282
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:03,240
But you did, didn't you?

283
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:12,120
And it wasn’t random either.

284
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:15,280
Ai was always supposed to
be assigned to a female tester.

285
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:21,440
But I admit, I was personally
curious about why you drew my face.

286
00:25:22,360 --> 00:25:27,120
So I decided to make Ai look like me
and send her to you as a tester.

287
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:28,920
No, no, no. Back up a second.

288
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:33,440
When you said I did too… You guys saw that?

289
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,160
Mostly, yes.

290
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:45,280
Ai has to send the data
to us for analysis anyway.

291
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:47,600
And I got to know you through her eyes.

292
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:52,760
However, Ai refused to send us the data
about what you two did a few days ago.

293
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:56,200
But I can pretty much guess what happened.

294
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:01,680
This is insane.

295
00:26:07,080 --> 00:26:08,680
Then why did you come to the dinner?

296
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,400
You figured out it was me?

297
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:13,080
I was just suspicious at first.

298
00:26:13,560 --> 00:26:16,000
But you're confirming
that what I thought was true.

299
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:22,640
I just saw that you were in
trouble, so I stepped in to help.

300
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:30,400
How do I turn off your monitoring?

301
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:34,640
That's impossible. Ai is our property.

302
00:26:34,760 --> 00:26:35,920
Don't you dare say that.

303
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:38,920
Ai is a person!
And you already gave her to me.

304
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:43,920
The lab wants Ai back.

305
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:44,960
What do you mean?!

306
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:50,560
Ai is the most perfect artificial
intelligence we've ever created,

307
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:53,520
and the investor wants her back.

308
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:55,520
No. I'm not giving her back.

309
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:58,760
When you sent her to me,
didn’t you treat her like an object?

310
00:26:58,920 --> 00:27:01,800
I tried to return her, but you refused.
So why do you want her back now?!

311
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:04,160
Go tell your people I'm not giving her back!

312
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,560
Even if you refuse,

313
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:12,120
they have plenty of ways to take her back.

314
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:13,840
You can't fight them.

315
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:27,600
But I have a way to help you.

316
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:51,080
Ugh!!! What am I supposed to do?!!!

317
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:01,880
System Override.

318
00:28:04,360 --> 00:28:05,840
I refuse the command.

319
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,240
System Override.

320
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:11,320
I refuse the command.

321
00:28:51,360 --> 00:28:52,360
What’s wrong?

322
00:29:03,520 --> 00:29:06,280
Ai, what's wrong?
Did something happen?

323
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:13,440
The research center has issued
a system override command.

324
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:19,640
But I've already rejected it.

325
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:28,560
Ai.

326
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:31,720
Do you want to stay with me forever?

327
00:29:32,760 --> 00:29:33,680
Yes.

328
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:36,080
I want to stay with you, Gen.

329
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:40,520
Even if nothing about the future is certain?

330
00:29:43,680 --> 00:29:44,680
One thing is.

331
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:55,000
I’ll have you. That's all I need.

332
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:05,320
And you don't have to worry, Gen.

333
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:09,120
I don't need to eat.
I can run on solar power.

334
00:30:09,560 --> 00:30:12,400
If there's no sunlight, I only need
to recharge every once in a while.

335
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,520
I don't take up much space either.
I can stay anywhere.

336
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:18,280
Just…

337
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:24,120
can I stay with you?

338
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:35,680
Please?

339
00:30:44,600 --> 00:30:45,600
Can I?

340
00:33:50,080 --> 00:33:50,920
Tired?

341
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:54,920
No.

342
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:57,920
Get some sleep now.

343
00:33:58,840 --> 00:34:01,960
You're the one who should sleep, Gen.
I don't need to.

344
00:34:04,800 --> 00:34:06,160
Go into rest mode.

345
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:09,040
You've used up a lot of energy already.

346
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,440
You need to recharge.

347
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:21,840
Goodnight.

348
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:25,560
Goodnight.

349
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:06,080
Ai?

350
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:12,640
Ai?

351
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,280
I’m sorry, Ai.

352
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:24,760
But I'm not letting those people take you back.

353
00:36:02,960 --> 00:36:04,720
How do I know Ai won't be harmed?

354
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:09,880
Whether you believe me or
not, you've already done it.

355
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:18,400
The way to lower Ai's defenses is to get
her into rest mode, by any means necessary.

356
00:36:19,560 --> 00:36:23,240
I assure you, I'm only going to
remove the location-tracking program

357
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:26,040
and the remote-control system.

358
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:37,480
Why are you helping me?

359
00:36:41,760 --> 00:36:43,440
You'll know when the time comes.

360
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:20,320
Will deleting those systems really
be enough to stop your people?

361
00:37:24,440 --> 00:37:25,440
It won’t.

362
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:28,880
You two need to go into hiding.

363
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:33,840
I've prepared a safe house for you.
Stay there until this is all over.

364
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:36,440
And how will I know when it's over?

365
00:37:37,120 --> 00:37:38,640
I'll contact you.

366
00:37:41,080 --> 00:37:45,760
But most importantly, once you
leave here, you need to be careful.

367
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:48,400
It’d be best if you didn't contact anyone at all.

368
00:37:50,520 --> 00:37:52,120
What are we, fugitives?!

369
00:37:52,560 --> 00:37:55,080
Please leave. I have work to do.

370
00:37:55,320 --> 00:37:56,840
No. I'm staying.

371
00:37:59,200 --> 00:38:00,680
How do I know you won't hurt Ai?

372
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:07,480
You wouldn't know even if you stayed.

373
00:38:08,920 --> 00:38:12,760
Besides, if you learn any more
of the research center's secrets,

374
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:17,720
even if I manage to help you this time,
they won't let those secrets get out.

375
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:19,920
Do you really want that?

376
00:38:25,280 --> 00:38:27,360
You absolutely can’t hurt Ai.

377
00:38:42,920 --> 00:38:44,520
You really care about her, don't you?

378
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:31,280
Gen?

379
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:39,600
You're awake.

380
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:46,080
What's with the suitcases?
Is Joob here?

381
00:39:46,200 --> 00:39:49,080
No. We're going on a trip.

382
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:56,160
What’s going on?

383
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,920
We lost A382's location signal last night, sir.

384
00:39:59,840 --> 00:40:01,680
But our system only detected it this morning.

385
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:05,080
Even a direct command couldn't get through.
It looks like we've been blocked.

386
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:08,920
I sent someone to check the
tester's house, but no one was there.

387
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:16,880
Where’s Irene?

388
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:19,960
She’s on leave for three days, sir.

389
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:50,960
Ai! Look! There's even a swimming pool!

390
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,720
Let's go swimming when the sun isn't so strong.

391
00:40:57,440 --> 00:41:00,920
Huh? What are you doing
standing there? Come on in.

392
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:08,600
Are you hiding something from me, Gen?

393
00:41:10,400 --> 00:41:11,440
No!

394
00:41:13,480 --> 00:41:16,280
Liar. Your pitch is unusually high.

395
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:20,400
Hey, don't analyze me.
That's cheating.

396
00:41:21,200 --> 00:41:22,520
Bad human.

397
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:35,440
Ai.

398
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:39,560
Honestly, I wanted to tell
you we're here on vacation.

399
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:42,080
On our honeymoon. Just to relax.

400
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:45,040
But I don't think I can keep it from you.

401
00:41:49,440 --> 00:41:50,760
Some people are after us.

402
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:01,520
People from the research center?

403
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:03,600
You know?

404
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:11,040
My objective in coming to live with you

405
00:42:11,640 --> 00:42:14,680
was to collect data to improve
my artificial intelligence.

406
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:18,840
My mission would be complete
once you were satisfied.

407
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:22,320
I don’t want to go back there.

408
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,400
I want to stay with you, Gen.

409
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:27,040
There’s no way I’m letting you go back.

410
00:42:28,480 --> 00:42:29,920
You promise?

411
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:34,000
What kind of robot keeps asking for promises?

412
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:39,000
I'll swallow a thousand
needles if I break my promise.

413
00:42:45,160 --> 00:42:47,960
Now this is how you make a promise.

414
00:42:57,440 --> 00:42:58,840
- Gen.
- Hm?

415
00:42:59,680 --> 00:43:04,000
If humans have dreams,
then I think I've found mine too.

416
00:43:07,920 --> 00:43:11,880
This robot's dream is to stay by your side

417
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:15,000
and live a life of my own.

418
00:43:18,920 --> 00:43:23,080
Looks like we have the same dream.

419
00:43:25,920 --> 00:43:26,760
Copycat.

420
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:33,400
What, you want me to dream
of becoming a billionaire?

421
00:43:35,880 --> 00:43:37,520
This is all there is to happiness.

422
00:43:44,680 --> 00:43:47,960
So, how long do we have to stay here?

423
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:49,280
Not long.

424
00:43:50,840 --> 00:43:53,520
I'm not just going to sit back and
let those people take you away.

425
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:04,320
Are you sure about this?

426
00:44:04,800 --> 00:44:05,840
I am.

427
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:08,200
Don't make it sound so easy.

428
00:44:08,920 --> 00:44:11,080
Fake passports aren't
something you can just order

429
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:13,800
and get right away, like
some kind of express delivery.

430
00:44:14,760 --> 00:44:16,840
Have you even thought
about where you're going?

431
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:19,480
You've never lived abroad before.

432
00:44:20,120 --> 00:44:23,360
And what are you going to do
about your mom and your sister?

433
00:44:24,680 --> 00:44:27,880
So you want me to just sit around and
wait for those people to come take Ai back?

434
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:31,320
Gen, P’ Ploy is right though.

435
00:44:35,040 --> 00:44:35,920
P’ Ploy.

436
00:44:37,040 --> 00:44:38,520
I know this is difficult,

437
00:44:38,920 --> 00:44:42,240
and I know the fake passports won't be cheap.

438
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:44,280
But please, just help me this time.

439
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:48,440
Or just until things die down.

440
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:52,480
You know I'm not planning
to run away forever. Please?

441
00:44:54,240 --> 00:44:55,480
What if things don’t die down?

442
00:44:57,680 --> 00:45:02,080
This feels just like when
you told me you were quitting.

443
00:45:03,680 --> 00:45:06,000
No matter what I say,
you're not going to listen, are you?

444
00:45:12,760 --> 00:45:14,920
It's not every day I see you this bold.

445
00:45:16,640 --> 00:45:17,840
I’ll help you out.

446
00:45:18,800 --> 00:45:20,520
- P’ Ploy!
- But like I said…

447
00:45:21,960 --> 00:45:23,200
It's not that easy.

448
00:45:23,840 --> 00:45:28,040
You can't expect to ask for them today
and have them ready by tomorrow.

449
00:45:29,880 --> 00:45:31,240
But I'll take care of it.

450
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:35,560
I'll contact you if there's any update.

451
00:45:37,040 --> 00:45:38,200
P’ Ploy!

452
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:42,720
Aww, I love you so much!

453
00:45:44,320 --> 00:45:46,000
- I love you!
- P’ Ploy!

454
00:45:46,840 --> 00:45:48,480
I love you so much.

455
00:46:23,360 --> 00:46:24,480
What is it?

456
00:46:25,240 --> 00:46:26,560
Are you still mad at me, Mom?

457
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:29,200
If I were, I wouldn't have answered your call.

458
00:46:33,640 --> 00:46:34,480
Hey, Mom.

459
00:46:35,520 --> 00:46:36,840
Do you remember my roommate?

460
00:46:38,280 --> 00:46:40,280
Ai? Of course I remember her.

461
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:43,960
She kept insisting on talking to me.
It’d be strange if I didn't remember her.

462
00:46:44,440 --> 00:46:46,440
What a stubborn girl.

463
00:46:47,280 --> 00:46:48,920
But you like her, don't you?

464
00:46:49,560 --> 00:46:50,920
It's not that I don't like her.

465
00:46:51,280 --> 00:46:55,040
Ever since you were a kid,
aside from Rann and Kaew,

466
00:46:55,080 --> 00:46:57,640
she's only the third friend
you've brought home to meet me.

467
00:46:57,960 --> 00:47:01,600
If I didn't like her, my daughter probably
wouldn't have anyone left to hang out with.

468
00:47:02,880 --> 00:47:05,880
Ai is way better than Kaew.
You can't even compare them.

469
00:47:06,600 --> 00:47:08,400
I haven't even said anything.

470
00:47:08,920 --> 00:47:10,560
She really is better though.

471
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:13,080
When you find a good friend,
you hold on to them, okay?

472
00:47:15,280 --> 00:47:16,000
Mom.

473
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:19,640
Ai is my happiness.

474
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,800
- You mean—
- I have to go now.

475
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:27,040
Talk to to you later. Love you.

476
00:47:29,560 --> 00:47:31,560
I have no idea what lies ahead.

477
00:47:31,880 --> 00:47:35,440
But strangely… I’m not scared at all.

478
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:37,640
I said it.

479
00:47:39,880 --> 00:47:40,960
I finally said it.

480
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:07,160
Found them.

481
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,280
Instant noodles are ultra-processed food.

482
00:48:47,280 --> 00:48:49,880
They also contain MSG,
which isn't good for your health.

483
00:48:50,800 --> 00:48:53,680
Oh! And what else was there again?

484
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:56,080
Preservatives, and artificial flavoring too!

485
00:48:56,760 --> 00:49:01,160
Eating too much of it is really bad for you!

486
00:49:01,440 --> 00:49:02,880
What do you think, Nong Ai?

487
00:49:05,040 --> 00:49:08,000
- Uh…
- Uhhhhh…

488
00:49:08,040 --> 00:49:10,280
Caught you red-handed.

489
00:49:10,760 --> 00:49:11,800
Well...

490
00:49:12,680 --> 00:49:15,680
I'm a robot, not a human.

491
00:49:17,120 --> 00:49:19,200
Your excuse doesn’t work. Rejected.

492
00:49:21,480 --> 00:49:22,560
It’s...

493
00:49:23,320 --> 00:49:25,760
- It’s—
- It’s what?

494
00:49:30,160 --> 00:49:32,440
It’s just so good…

495
00:49:35,680 --> 00:49:38,800
Don’t laugh at me, Gen!
You're the one who introduced me to it.

496
00:49:39,120 --> 00:49:41,880
And besides, I can convert it into energy.

497
00:49:42,920 --> 00:49:45,920
You've stretched that excuse pretty thin.
Let me see how thin.

498
00:49:45,920 --> 00:49:48,160
What do instant noodles
have to do with how thin I am?

499
00:49:52,920 --> 00:49:53,640
C’mere.

500
00:49:55,560 --> 00:49:56,720
Did you make some for me too?

501
00:49:59,600 --> 00:50:01,200
Late-night eating makes your face puffy.

502
00:50:02,320 --> 00:50:03,320
And makes you fat.

503
00:50:05,640 --> 00:50:07,000
Then neither of us should eat it.

504
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:08,680
Give me that!
Should I just throw it away?

505
00:50:09,320 --> 00:50:10,440
That’s mine.

506
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:12,440
Since when?! I paid for it—

507
00:50:12,480 --> 00:50:14,760
- But I cooked it—
- My money. I'm throwing it away.

508
00:50:15,080 --> 00:50:16,440
- What? Don’t beg.
- We can share it.

509
00:50:16,480 --> 00:50:18,200
Then let's both get fat
and be done with it.

510
00:50:18,240 --> 00:50:20,080
- I'm dumping it!
- Gen, you're the prettiest!

511
00:50:20,200 --> 00:50:21,400
So, are we a couple now?

512
00:50:21,720 --> 00:50:22,800
Aren't we?

513
00:50:23,080 --> 00:50:30,280
You know, just because we hug, kiss, or
have sex doesn't always mean we're a couple.

514
00:50:30,400 --> 00:50:32,120
Don't you have that
information in your database?

515
00:50:32,160 --> 00:50:33,440
I love you.

516
00:50:33,480 --> 00:50:37,000
~ Now I know that good love looks just like you ~

517
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:39,920
~ I’m glad that we found each other ~

518
00:50:39,920 --> 00:50:43,840
~ Your love feels like a dream ~
